  "finding": "Personally inspected all 14 raw source and battle sheets from five complete face angles including chin and underside plus two body angles, all eight low and medium runtime sheets, all 216 actual battle technique frames, nine original contact/framing frames, 24 advancing idle frames and all 16 atlas cells. Blue muzzle, yellow eyes, nostrils and cream chin retain coherent shape; the cream throat broadens with neck flexion but remains continuous beneath the muzzle, with the dark lapels occluding the lower throat in bent poses. Headband plate, ties, torso, upper arms, hands, legs and webbed feet remain attached through locomotion, jump, strike, death and revival. Water Strike front and side at .16/.24/.36 seconds keep the webbed feet above the platform; side .60 Water Strike, Water Breaker and signature preserve the full head, ties and body within the frame. No visible disconnected motion, torn face or platform penetration found in the explicitly sampled scope.",
